<title>USA: Sioux Falls hogs off $1.75 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Sioux Falls hogs off $1.75 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SIOUX FALLS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said barrows and gilts were $1.75 lower. Trading was fairly active. Top $50.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    220-260 lbs   50.00-50.50</p>
<p>		  260-270 lbs   49.50-50.00</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-280 lbs   48.50-49.50</p>
<p>		  280-290 lbs   47.50-48.50</p>
<p>    US 3-4    290-300 lbs   46.50-47.50</p>
<p>Sows - off $1.00-3.00. Top $48.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    300-400 lbs    43.50-43.75</p>
<p>		  400-450 lbs    few 44.50, but not fully tested</p>
<p>		  450-500 lbs    few 45.00, but lightly tested</p>
<p>		  500-650 lbs    46.00-48.00</p>
</text>
